Switchyard patch 0002 (app/scripts/patch-exact.sh applies it): the native canvas seam stops making
per-frame garbage that Hermes counts as external memory. Each canvas's list writer is reused across
frames (no 256 B -> doubling ArrayBuffer chain per frame), base64 goes into one reused byte buffer
and becomes strings 4 KB at a time, and the reply is joined once around them (no `out +=` four
characters at a time, no second copy through JSON.stringify). The reply's bytes are identical
(checked against the unpatched seam on 78 replies: empty, 1-40000 ops, sealed lists, text, throws).
The web's seam (host/web-js/ts-draw.js) keeps `take()` and is untouched.

--- a/canvas/recorder.js
+++ b/canvas/recorder.js
@@ -480,6 +480,9 @@
     this.len = need; this.ops++;
   }
   finish() { return new Uint8Array(this.buf, 0, this.len); }
+  // Switchyard patch (app/scripts/exact-patches/0002): the native seam encodes the list and
+  // records the next frame into the same buffer, so a canvas stops growing a fresh one per frame.
+  reset() { this.len = 8; this.ops = 0; }
 }
 
